@*
    The hero.

    Restructured rather than restyled. It used to be a text column beside a product column,
    which is the arrangement every hosting company on the internet has, and which forced the
    headline into roughly half the page - at display sizes that meant the type ran into the
    panel next to it.

    Here the headline takes the full measure and everything else sits underneath it: the lede
    and the actions on the left, one rack unit on the right. The headline gets to be as large
    as it deserves, the two columns below it are short enough that neither crowds the other,
    and the page reads top to bottom the way an editorial spread does rather than left to
    right the way a template does.

    No ambient field behind it any more. Light comes from one source, declared once on the
    page ground - see the body::before note in app.css.
*@

@inject IStringLocalizer<HomeText> Text

<section class="hero" id="top" data-stage>
    <div class="hts-container hts-container--wide hero-inner">
        <p class="hero-kicker" data-text-effect="flicker">
            <span class="kicker-rule"></span>
            @Text["Hero.Kicker"]
        </p>

        @*
            All three lines are white. The emphasis is weight, not colour: 460 against 800 in
            the same family is a strong enough contrast to carry a headline on its own, and it
            leaves purple free to mean what it means everywhere else on the site - running, or
            the one thing this page wants you to press.
        *@
        <h1 class="hero-title" data-text-effect="rise">
            <span class="title-line">@Text["Hero.Line1"]</span>
            <span class="title-line title-line--accent">@Text["Hero.Line2"]</span>
            <span class="title-line">@Text["Hero.Line3"]</span>
        </h1>

        <div class="hero-body">
            <div class="hero-copy-col">
                <p class="hero-copy">@Text["Hero.Copy"]</p>

                <div class="hero-actions">
                    <CtaButton Href="/project-zomboid" Size="CtaSize.Large" TrailingIcon="IconName.ArrowRight">
                        @Text["Hero.CtaPrimary"]
                    </CtaButton>
                    <CtaButton Href="#control-panel" Variant="CtaVariant.Secondary" Size="CtaSize.Large">
                        @Text["Hero.CtaSecondary"]
                    </CtaButton>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="hero-panel-col">
                <HeroPanel />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hts-container hts-container--wide hero-foot">
        <span class="foot-coord">@Text["Hero.FootCell"]</span>
        <span class="foot-scroll">
            <span class="foot-scroll-track"><span class="foot-scroll-dot"></span></span>
            @Text["Hero.FootScroll"]
        </span>
        <span class="foot-alloc">@Text["Hero.FootAllocation"]</span>
    </div>
</section>

